45 "We identify the leading term of the polynomial and compute its limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }(4-{x}^{2}) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }(-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-(\\infty ) \\\\  & =-\\infty \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264561 13194139533899 true] [17592186264560 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533899 true] [17592186264560 1041 "field-1" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264560 1104 #edb/ref 17592186264561 13194139533899 true] [17592186264560 1110 #uuid "958887a5-800c-57f0-977f-c87b76df8b8c" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264561 1034 "-\\infty" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533899 true] [17592186264561 1111 #uuid "b7e93ad7-3079-55cc-a243-3df0165226b6" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264562 1017 #edb/ref 17592186264563 13194139533899 true] [17592186264562 1089 "q-166217" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264562 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533899 true] [17592186264562 1100 "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nEvaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}.$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264562 1113 #uuid "386145e1-97c4-5291-9ae5-69c49e55606b" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264562 1145 "If we attempt to evaluate the limit directly by substituting $x=2,$ we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{4-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}}{4-{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since there is a radical in the numerator, we can evaluate the limit by first multiplying the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{f(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x}}{4-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{(\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{x})(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})}{(4-{x}^{2})(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{2-x}{(2+x)(2-x)(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{\\cancel{2-x}}{(2+x)\\cancel{(2-x)}(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}\\frac{1}{(2+x)(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(2+2)(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4(2\\sqrt{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264563 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264564 13194139533899 true] [17592186264563 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533899 true] [17592186264563 1041 "field-1" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264563 1104 #edb/ref 17592186264564 13194139533899 true] [17592186264563 1110 #uuid "4ad08d2e-4cb8-52a6-b31d-060fd0512bde" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264564 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533899 true] [17592186264564 1111 #uuid "58d9e57e-f446-5415-8893-879950cf8d7e" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264565 1017 #edb/ref 17592186264566 13194139533899 true] [17592186264565 1089 "q-166218" 13194139533899 true] [17592186264565 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533899 true] [17592186264565 1100 "Consider the quadratic function $f(x)=4-{x}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x).$ If the limit does not exist, write \"DNE\" (without the quotation marks).\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }f(x)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\infty$\n\nEarlier part 2